WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.140
This is a table of counts. In about a minute it's going to write a sentence that nobody has ever written.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:15.840
Each row is a word from a book, and the tallies say which words came next, and how often. It's the same kind of grid you just filled in.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:27.300
A story starts after a full stop, so start at the row for full stop. After a full stop, the book has "it" seven times, "here" four, "down" three, "swoop" three.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:41.960
Now pick the next word at random, with a ten-sided die. Seventeen tallies don't split into ten faces exactly, so share them as fairly as you can: "it" gets four faces, the others two each.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:52.940
Roll a two. That's in the band for "it". Write the word down, and go to the row for "it".

00:00:53.770 --> 00:01:02.440
The row for "it" has exactly ten tallies, so every tally gets one face. Roll a one: "sits".

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:10.240
"Sits" is only ever followed by "on", and "on" by "the". One option, no roll.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:27.160
The row for "the" shares its faces four ways. Roll a nine: "dog". And after "dog", a full stop or "runs", five faces each. Roll a three: full stop.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:36.620
"It sits on the dog." The book never says that; the magpie sits on the fence. Nobody wrote this sentence; the counting did.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:40.580
And here's everything this model could have written instead.

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:47.500
Every roll picks a different path. So run it ten thousand times and count what comes out.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:02:00.190
Every text different. Every text sounding like the book. That's what Claude or ChatGPT is doing every time it writes a word, with vastly more counts than this.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:17.540
On your grid: pick any starting word with a row and write it down. Share the die's faces across its row by the tallies, roll, and write down the word you land on. Then find its row. No row? Pick a new word and carry on.

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.380
Pick a starting word and roll.
